  "not_simulated": [
    {
      "what": "data output",
      "pins": ["DOUT"],
      "why": "The ws2812 kind has no DOUT pin. Section 11 gives the DIN to DOUT delay as 500 ns maximum, and a one-LED part discards the bits past its own 24."
    },
    {
      "what": "supply and current",
      "why": "Section 8 lists VDD from +3.7 V to +5.5 V. The ESP32-S3-DevKitC-1 ties this LED to 3.3 V, which is below that range, and the kind does not check the supply. Section 9 names SK6805MINI-HS at 5 mA and SK6812MINI-HS at 12 mA. Section 10's static IDD typical is 1 mA. The part does not pick one of those currents."
    },
    {
      "what": "bit times",
      "why": "The kind uses the Worldsemi WS2812E-1313 V1.1 windows, a 0 for a high of 220 ns to 380 ns and a 1 for 580 ns to 1 us. Section 12 of this sheet gives T0H as 0.2 / 0.32 / 0.4 us and T1H as 0.62 / 0.64 / 1.0 us, and section 11 gives fDIN typical 800 kHz. The typical highs sit inside those windows. T0H maximum, 0.4 us, does not."
    }
  ]
}
